Cell["\<\
Use the three-point QED model for diagrams and the QED model containing the \
known four-point amplitudes for five-point factorization. Neither model is \
changed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e40be2b8-a07c-4c47-93ff-40449897d0a0"],

Cell["\<\
diagramModel = ReadModel[FileNameJoin[{hepcatDirectory, \"models\"}], 2];
factorizationModel = ReadModel[FileNameJoin[{hepcatDirectory, \"models\"}], 3];
electronMass = ModelParameter[diagramModel, \"Me\"];
electricCharge = ModelParameter[diagramModel, \"EE\"];
timeLimit = 180;
checkSamples = 2;\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f61894d2-c74b-4610-a3de-e1941760c4ae"],

Cell["\<\
The independent benchmark uses the massive-QED Feynman model. Its own model \
file specifies the same numerical electron mass and charge as the \
constructive QED example. Each model retains its own parameters; no global \
parameter assignments or symbol substitutions are needed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5e949351-7167-4e81-83a5-e5d0eebf69c2"],

Cell["\<\
qedFeynmanModel = ReadModel[FileNameJoin[{hepcatDirectory, \
\"model_feynman\"}], 2];\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:=",ExpressionUUID->"39ecf8f2-3357-45c7-b69b-99fa03763f4d"],

Cell["\<\
The amplitudes retain symbolic Me and EE. Numerical checks and completion use \
the parameter values and derived functions from the supplied model. PASS \
means agreement at the tested samples, not a general analytic proof.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"43f1ccea-2be0-4dac-abdd-f6a191035779"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["e,E,A.+,A.+,A.+", "Chapter",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001759665590519*^9, 
  4.00175967079949*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4254fc93-7cf4-42a6-a5cc-\
47271d455e72"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Choose the Process and References", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a25b4f6c-ab7e-4178-82c7-1af73d66324e"],

Cell["\<\
Start with the all-plus example. To explore another process, change particles \
and reevaluate Sections 1-5. Completion supplements sewn channels with verified \
reference alternatives without changing the prepared diagrams. It refits failed \
validation samples within explicit limits. A bounded correction space can still \
be insufficient; UNRESOLVED is not a completed amplitude. Existing worked \
derivations are shown separately below.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"884df899-0624-455e-ac77-ff3789ad9b73"],

Cell["\<\
particles = {\"e\", \"E\", \"A.+\", \"A.+\", \"A.+\"};
referenceChoice = \"AllSpurious\";\
\>", "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0016723486207333`*^9, 4.001672391849534*^9}, {
   4.001757782755148*^9, 4.00175778752351*^9}, 4.001757993489561*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[11]:=",ExpressionUUID->"59e9054c-37eb-4d9b-9009-ab266ff680e0"],

Cell["\<\
Other examples are {\"e\",\"E\",\"A.+\",\"A.+\",\"A.-\"} and {\"e\",\"E\",\"E\
\",\"e\",\"A.+\"}. Reference choices: Automatic; \"AllSpurious\" (cyclic \
other massless particles); \"AllPhysical\" (momentum-insertion references \
outside the diagram's own poles); \"Xi\" (one common Xi0); \"IndependentXi\"; \
\"ReverseCyclic\"; None (unchanged). The referenceChoice variable controls \
the preparation in Section 3.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"381d17af-a09d-4116-8fd8-3524916bcd57"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2. Generate the Diagrams", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"db43e89f-6886-4c59-b8e6-bfcf66576fc6"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
diagrams = CreateDiagrams[particles, diagramModel];
rawAmplitudes = diagramAmplitudes[diagrams];
Length[rawAmplitudes]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[13]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2cf0490d-3446-4e8f-8f1f-5f2d05171f2d"],

Cell[BoxData["6"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0016721377967997`*^9, 4.0016879511169777`*^9, 
  4.0020168126609573`*^9, 4.002021500272408*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[15]=",ExpressionUUID->"4cb99b28-bba2-44af-a6a1-a18e6ce4afe2"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The all-plus process has six diagrams. rawAmplitudes keeps each expression \
together with that diagram's mass rules.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"99bed7d4-df64-4bc9-a7e3-460737ceb805"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["View the diagrams", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"f30e05cf-6e77-4326-97b4-d9c6741dc99e"],

Cell["CreateArrowDiagrams[diagrams]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e6e7e4e9-1352-4ac9-8f16-31a663ee659e"]
}, Closed]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3. Prepare Each Diagram", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d7eb1abf-cdef-4adf-b490-a6d9f152e8a2"],

Cell["\<\
Preparation applies ReduceSpinContractions, selects the references, reduces \
known numerator scalar products, calls ReduceSpinorProducts, then continues \
with improving identity steps. Each diagram uses its own internal on-shell \
conditions in its numerator. Original propagators stay off shell.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a7164525-9dfc-4fd1-ae72-3cb18a63da1c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
preparation = PrepareAmplitudes[rawAmplitudes, diagramModel,
  \"ReferenceSpinors\" -> referenceChoice];
preparation\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ec1714ca-a64e-4304-b156-d264fbcc9cb0"],

